Vendored third-party dependency, moved to soroban-sdk 29
========================================================

  Library:  soroban-poseidon 28.0.0 (Rust, no_std)
  Upstream: https://github.com/stellar/rs-soroban-poseidon
  Release:  crates.io soroban-poseidon 28.0.0 (.crate sha256
            9d3c971964bbff3b7f716b251e3cd8caa71ab4fbe33aa8fc845570dcdbe97582),
            published from commit 521da986541843a5cd1a94f36f681f14bdad3b90
            ("Bump version to 28.0.0 (#19)")
  License:  Apache-2.0 (see LICENSE)
  Used by:  perch-zk-primitives (Poseidon2 on the host)

Why vendored
------------
soroban-poseidon 28.0.0, its newest release, requires soroban-sdk ^28, and
no upstream branch moves it to 29 (checked 2026-11-03). Its src/ is
byte-identical to 27.0.0, the release perch used before. Perch builds with
soroban-sdk 29.0.1 / soroban-env-host 29.0.1, and a crate that requires
another soroban-sdk major cannot share its types, so this copy is built as a
path dependency with the soroban-sdk pin moved. No change was proposed
upstream.

Upstream files
--------------
Every file is upstream's bytes except Cargo.toml (the published, normalized
manifest), whose delta is below. UPSTREAM.sha256 lists the sha256 of every
vendored file as published.

Not vendored: Cargo.lock, Cargo.toml.orig, Makefile, CONTRIBUTING.md,
RELEASING.md, rust-toolchain.toml.

SDK 29 delta
------------
Cargo.toml only:

  - `[dependencies.soroban-sdk]` version "28.0.0" became "29.0.1";
  - the `[dev-dependencies]` table was dropped (the tests are not vendored),
    and so was `[profile.release]`, which cargo ignores in a dependency and
    warns about.

The source builds unchanged: soroban-sdk 29 has no API changes from 28
(soroban-sdk's own migration notes: "Migrating from v28 to v29: None").

Updating
--------
Replace the directory with the new upstream files, re-apply the delta above,
regenerate UPSTREAM.sha256 from the unmodified upstream files, and update
this NOTICE. crates/integration-tests/tests/vendor.rs requires every
vendored file other than Cargo.toml to hash to UPSTREAM.sha256 (after
reversing any source delta above) and the directory to hold nothing else but
NOTICE and UPSTREAM.sha256, so no other upstream byte can change unnoticed.
